Permission for Course Use

Students, teaching assistants, and instructors of CSE 3666 at the University
of Connecticut are permitted to use, copy, and modify this software and its
accompanying instructional materials for educational purposes in the course.
This permission includes running the software, keeping private working copies
and backups, and submitting coursework through university-approved systems.

Authorized Sharing

Course participants may share the materials and their modifications privately
with authorized course instructors and teaching assistants. Assignments are
individual work. Sharing with other students or any other person requires
express authorization from the instructor, subject to the course policy.
Course staff may distribute the materials privately to authorized course
participants. These permissions do not authorize public distribution.

Restrictions on Redistribution

Except as expressly permitted above or authorized in writing by the copyright
holder, recipients may not redistribute this software, the accompanying
instructional materials, or modified versions of those materials. In
particular, recipients may not post them in public repositories, on websites,
in online forums, on public file-sharing services, or through any other
publicly accessible service. Sharing with tutors or other third parties
requires prior written permission unless they are authorized course
participants acting within the permissions above.

These restrictions continue after completion of the course. Private retention
of course materials and completed work for personal reference is permitted.
The purpose of the public-posting restriction is to preserve the learning
opportunity for future students.

This license does not claim ownership of students' independently authored
work. Sharing or publishing assignment solutions, including independently
written solutions, is also governed by the course academic-integrity and
solution-sharing policies, which apply separately from this license.

Adoption in Other Courses

Instructors who wish to adopt or distribute this project in other courses
must obtain prior written permission from the copyright holder, for example
by email.

